: true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "⅜", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I compare fractions and decimals?", "p": ["Step 1: Fractions: find a common denominator, compare numerators.", "Step 2: Decimals: compare digits from the left.", "Step 3: Mixed forms: change to all decimals (or all fractions).", "Step 4: Use < and > correctly."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order fractions", "p": [], "q": "Order ½, ⅖, 7/10.", "steps": [["tenths: 5/10, 4/10, 7/10", ""]], "a": "⅖, ½, 7/10"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order decimals", "p": [], "q": "Order 0.4, 0.38, 0.45.", "steps": [["0.40, 0.38, 0.45", ""]], "a": "0.38, 0.4, 0.45"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Mixed", "p": [], "q": "Which is bigger: ¾ or 0.7?", "steps": [["¾ = 0.75", ""]], "a": "¾"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Same numerator", "p": [], "q": "Compare ⅖ and ⅔ (same numerator 2).", "steps": [["fifths are smaller than thirds", ""]], "a": "⅔"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Decimals", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u07s3t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Smallest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "0.09", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "0.1", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "0.19", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Bigger denominator means bigger", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Compare ⅙ and ¼.", "lines": ["6 > 4, so ⅙ is bigger"], "bad": 0, "why": "Sixths are SMALLER pieces than quarters: ⅙ < ¼.", "fix": [["⅙ < ¼", ""]], "id": "m5u07s3t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Thinking a bigger denominator means a bigger fraction", "p": ["More pieces → each piece is smaller."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Recipes, sports results (0.4 s vs 0.38 s) and sales compare fractions and decimals."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Common denominator → compare numerators.", "Same numerator → smaller denominator is bigger.", "Decimals: compare from the left.", "Change to one form for mixed comparisons."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 66